msgid "The AST is uploaded with the run, for that ref's own review; the shared cache is left alone."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/ig-ast-cache.bpmn:93
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The runner mounts the layers the IG repository's `index.lock.json` pins, restores and judges the cache itself, and, when it is not valid, runs the caller's optional `pre-export` overlay command, then `AstExportCli` (Tool `ig-ast-export`, `litlfred/fhir-ig-publisher` at the pinned `claude/ast-export` commit) with `-tx`. The inputs `pre-export` changed are put back and the AST is recorded against the clean commit's input digest (`ig-ast.ts source-inputs`). The AST just built must itself be `valid` for the commit, or the run fails."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/ig-ast-cache.bpmn:72
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The site route's steps, provided by the mounted layers and run by `stage-local.ts` → `build-instance-site.ts`: the landing layer's IG API sidecars when it has the step (`ig-site:sidecars`), the artefact index from the AST and the thin pages with the IG composed at the root (`ig-site:compose`: `ast-to-artifact-index.ts`, `gen-ig-pages.ts --compiled-data ast-data`), the OpenAPI pages when the IG holds them (`ig-site:openapi`), the AST's resources served as `ast-data/` and the build stamp (`ig-site:publisher-pages`). Published at the root from the default branch, as a preview otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/ig-ast-cache.bpmn:81
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The site says what built it (`folio-build.json`), and every artefact page carries the AST's provisional mark."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/ig-ast-cache.bpmn:29
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Wants the IG's site published, and is the only one who starts a runner: dispatching `ig-ast-refresh.yml` spends Actions minutes and writes a shared branch, so an agent never dispatches it on its own (`feature-staging` §\"Agent-run repositories\"). Accountable for asking for the refresh when the publish refuses a stale AST, rather than for publishing around it."
msgstr ""

